#Ship Classes
; Sathanas counterplay. Only the SJ Sathanas is named here, and only its flags change.
; core/tools/test_sathanas_counterplay.py audits this file.
;
; The engine gives a ship with the "supercap" flag a fixed share of the damage that guns,
; missiles and torpedoes would do (a quarter), and none at all once its hull is at or below
; 75%, unless the weapon itself carries the "supercap" flag. Only two retail weapons do, and
; no fleet carries them, so a Sathanas could not be brought below 75% hull by any fleet in
; play. Beams are not affected by that rule.
;
; Retail lists ("supercap" "big damage"). A $Flags line without +noreplace replaces the whole
; set, so this one lists everything the Sathanas keeps: "capital" in place of "supercap" (the
; Lucifer's class), "big damage" as retail has it, and the "generate icon" that
; fs2rts-pilot-icons-shp.tbm adds, so the result does not depend on which table loads first.
; The Colossus and Hades are not named and keep their flags.
;
; Hull is 300,000 (retail 1,000,000). Fleet groups sent at a Sathanas in
; core/tools/supercap_hunt_probe.lua took 394 (8 bombers) to 876 (8 bombers and 12 fighters)
; hull per second off the retail hull. Once the Sathanas reaches a station's guns the station
; has about 450 s, and a fleet needs about 150 s to answer, so a committed group of 16 bombers
; (758/s) has to finish it inside about 600 s: 300,000 / 758 = 396 s. The engine reads
; $Hitpoints before $Flags in a ship entry, so it has to stay in this order.
$Name: SJ Sathanas
+nocreate
$Hitpoints: 300000
$Flags: ("capital" "big damage" "generate icon")

#End
